            <ArticleTitle>Electrical brain stimulation for the control of chronic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>88-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An implanted brain stimulation system can be used for control of chronic intractable pain that is unresponsive to other forms of treatment. A trial period of temporary stimulation first determines whether a patient is likely to benefit from a permanent implant. Success has been achieved in the majority of patients, although technical problems have necessitated repairs.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
